  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The optical path between any two points is proportional to the time of travel.</p><p>The distance traversed by light in a medium of refractive index&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;in time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>vt</mi></math>&nbsp;.......(i)</p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math>&nbsp;is velocity of light in the medium. The distance traversed by light in a vacuum in this time,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;[from equation (i)]</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;d</mi></math>&nbsp;.....(ii) (Since<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfrac></math>)</p><p>This distance is the equivalent distance in vacuum and is called optical path.</p><p>Here, optical path for first ray&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>Optical path for second ray&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Path difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Now, phase difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo></math>path difference</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
